Package: xios-fhs
Name: Xios filesystem + hardware bridge
Version: 1.0.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Author: Max Leiter <maxwell.leiter@gmail.com>
Depends: libglib2.0-0
Provides: xios-hwbridge
Section: X11
Priority: optional
Description: Standard Linux paths + battery/brightness for the Xios desktop
 Makes the rootless iOS filesystem present the layout desktop software expects,
 and bridges the hardware it reads there. Lays down a synthetic /var/jb/sys with
 backlight and power-supply nodes and an os-release, then runs xios-hwbridged: a
 small session daemon that owns org.freedesktop.UPower (so the GNOME battery
 indicator and low-battery notifications work, backed by IOKit power sources) and
 applies screen-brightness writes through BackBoardServices, keeping the synthetic
 backlight tree in sync with Control Center. No per-app hacks: the shell and
 gnome-settings-daemon talk their normal D-Bus and sysfs interfaces.
